# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# h.env: what r6-held part H expects on the laptop.  Sourced by lib_h.sh on the laptop and by stage_h.sh / freeze_h.sh on the Mac.
# ~/sgxfive-test-rgn4: built from resgx545 r3-rgn4 4623753 (sgxfive-test.c sha256 703cbcea..., TOOLSRC.sha256), the tool of E848's
# cells, unchanged; a tool with another sha256 or a module that is not the expected build: STOP AND ASK (nothing is rebuilt).
TOOL_SHA=e6951558a93b4b7bc750eeae302997992d7ec6e26719bc527ba1ffc9c6fb779a
# the gma500 module of fork r6-kernel 3f0b3e74 (rgn4 + render_tail_room + peek + bif_flush), the lead's cachix build of 2026-11-12
# (vermagic 7.3.0-resgx545 SMP preempt mod_unload 686, gma500_gfx.ko sha256 8a32dada...): loaded = installed = this
SRCV_EXPECT=41E2F5C756F96D20F7109A4
# a job (640 x 480 at most)
JOB_TIMEOUT=${JOB_TIMEOUT:-120}
# a step of a cell (a fill or a 64 x 64 triangle; a replay fault is recovered by the kernel within about 1.5 s, E848)
STEP_TIMEOUT=${STEP_TIMEOUT:-60}
# the held jobs: the registers are read HOLD_READ s after the launch (E444, E848: 2.8 s), again HOLD_GAP s later, [the flush], then
# the kernel's own debugfs reset with the hold still Y; the job is bounded by HELD_TIMEOUT
HOLD_READ=${HOLD_READ:-2.8}
HOLD_GAP=${HOLD_GAP:-1}
HELD_TIMEOUT=${HELD_TIMEOUT:-60}
# free space on ~ before each job (MiB; HACKING's floor is 200): a job keeps well under 1 MB of gzipped logs and registers
MIN_FREE_MB=${MIN_FREE_MB:-300}
